WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.260
How does a developer get from biology classes
in Kerala

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:05.970
to reading the marks on a centuries-old palm
leaf?

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.490
For Adarsh, the journey began in school.

00:00:09.113 --> 00:00:11.874
He completed high school at MGM in Engapuzha,

00:00:11.874 --> 00:00:16.475
then studied biology at Government Higher
Secondary School in Thamarassery.

00:00:17.113 --> 00:00:20.043
At the College of Applied Science in
Thamarassery,

00:00:20.043 --> 00:00:22.153
he earned a computer science degree.

00:00:22.153 --> 00:00:26.321
Programming and databases became his
foundation for building software.

00:00:26.947 --> 00:00:29.826
His master's at Government Engineering
College,

00:00:29.826 --> 00:00:32.276
Thrissur, brought those skills together.

00:00:32.276 --> 00:00:36.886
He applied computer vision to photo privacy
and to reading handwritten manuscripts.

00:00:37.488 --> 00:00:40.759
At Bluegen Solutions, he built Django
endpoints for

00:00:40.759 --> 00:00:44.351
authenticated requests and designed linked
MySQL tables.

00:00:44.351 --> 00:00:48.368
Debugging with the team taught him to trace an
issue from request to database.

00:00:48.988 --> 00:00:52.130
At The Skybrisk, he built React components for

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:55.409
product catalogs, purchase orders, and
invoices.

00:00:55.409 --> 00:00:59.814
He connected them to APIs, managed state with
Redux Toolkit,

00:00:59.814 --> 00:01:02.016
and added PDF invoice exports.

00:01:02.655 --> 00:01:06.800
His DevOps internship at CODTECH took him into
software delivery.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.082
He automated builds and tests in GitHub
Actions,

00:01:10.082 --> 00:01:14.800
configured Kubernetes deployments, and added
baseline security scans.

00:01:15.405 --> 00:01:18.081
His published paper asks how software can read

00:01:18.081 --> 00:01:20.874
inkless writing carved into damaged palm
leaves.

00:01:20.874 --> 00:01:23.990
It describes checking the leaf's surface and
using adaptive

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:26.842
thresholding to separate faint grooves from
the grain.

00:01:27.447 --> 00:01:30.665
The paper explores transformer-based
transcription.

00:01:30.665 --> 00:01:35.145
The public prototype uses geometric features
and a Malayalam word list.

00:01:35.145 --> 00:01:38.294
A next step is to test a trained recognizer on

00:01:38.294 --> 00:01:41.717
held-out manuscripts and measure character
errors.

00:01:42.322 --> 00:01:46.607
Across these experiences, Adarsh learned to
connect an interface,

00:01:46.607 --> 00:01:50.101
a database, an image pipeline, and a release
process.

00:01:50.101 --> 00:01:53.353
He wants to bring those skills to a software
engineering team.
